WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:16.840
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:21.010
to air in 2022.
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:26.360
as showrunners and executive producers. George
R. R. Martin will also serve as executive

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.860
producer.
It is based on George RR Martin’s book Fire

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:33.700
And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s yet unfinished
Fire And Blood volume 2 book.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:38.160
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator of

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.800
the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount the
generations of Targaryens who fought to hold

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:47.920
that iconic seat, all the way up to the civil
war that nearly tore their dynasty apart.”

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:52.280
That's Fire And Blood volume 1.
The yet unreleased Fire And Blood volume 2

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:58.200
will continue from where part 1 ended, with
Rhaenyra Targaryen's son Aegon lll's reign

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:03.320
and will cover Blackyre rebellions, war with
Dorne and go all the way to the Mad King and

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:09.170
Robert's Rebellion that ended Targaryen dynasty.
Ned Stark's older brother, Brandon Stark,

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:12.610
played a big role in the prelude to Robert's
Rebellion.

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:17.119
Brandon Stark was the heir of Rickard Stark,
the Lord of Winterfell, and the older brother

00:01:17.119 --> 00:01:22.310
of Eddard, Lyanna and Benjen Stark. He was
killed by strangulation by the Mad King

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:27.110
when he protested the kidnapping of Lyanna
by Prince Rhaegar Targaryen.

00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:32.620
His father Rickard died along with him by
wildfire. This brutal act triggered Robert's

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:35.459
Rebellion,
the civil war that led to the removal of House

00:01:35.459 --> 00:01:39.870
Targaryen from the Iron Throne.
Originally, Game of Thrones season 1 was to

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:43.220
feature a scene where the Mad King executes
the Starks.

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:48.350
It was filmed and put in the trailer, but
they eventually decided to edit it out.

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:51.840
Brandon was in appearance and character very
different from Eddard.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:57.380
He had grey eyes, and was tall and handsome.
Brandon was absolutely not shy about taking

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:02.179
what he wanted.
He was rather hot-blooded, a trait their father,

00:02:02.179 --> 00:02:06.310
Lord Rickard, described as originating from
"the wolf blood".

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:10.560
Brandon shared this trait with his sister,
Lyanna, and Eddard believes this led them

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:16.470
both to early deaths. Brandon was the best
swordsman among his siblings, and an excellent

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:19.940
jouster.
He loved to hone his sword, preferring it

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:24.000
to be as sharp as possible. He also loved
to ride.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:29.230
Born in 262 AC at Winterfell, Brandon was
the eldest son and heir of Lord Rickard and

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:33.069
Lady Lyarra Stark.
Rickard was the head of House Stark and Lord

00:02:33.069 --> 00:02:36.659
Paramount of the North,
the Warden of the North and head of House

00:02:36.659 --> 00:02:41.000
Stark until he was executed
along with his eldest son and heir Brandon

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:46.060
by the Mad King, Aerys II Targaryen.
The North is one of the constituent regions

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:49.230
of the Seven Kingdoms
and House Stark is one of the Great Houses

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:52.530
of the realm.
House Stark rules the region from their seat

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:57.549
of Winterfell
and Rickard also held the title Lord of Winterfell.

00:02:57.549 --> 00:03:01.189
Rickard was the father of Brandon, Eddard,
Lyanna and Benjen Stark.

00:03:01.189 --> 00:03:05.770
Both Rickard Stark and the Mad King are grandfathers
to Jon Snow.

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:09.520
Rickard Stark served faithfully under King
Aerys II.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:14.719
He was saved from drowning by Ser Arthur Dayne
during the siege of White Harbor by the outlaw

00:03:14.719 --> 00:03:20.640
Sea Kings. He arranged for the betrothal of
his daughter Lyanna Stark to Robert Baratheon,

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:26.349
the Lord Paramount of the Stormlands. He also
betrothed his son and heir Brandon Stark to

00:03:26.349 --> 00:03:31.370
Catelyn Tully, the daughter of Hoster Tully,
Lord Paramount of the Riverlands.

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:35.969
Both engagements were broken when Prince Rhaegar
Targaryen abducted Lyanna.

00:03:35.969 --> 00:03:38.999
Brandon was fostered at Barrowton with Lord
Dustin.

00:03:38.999 --> 00:03:44.010
He spent most his time riding in the Rills.
His father betrothed him to Catelyn Tully

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:49.650
of Riverrun , who considered him to be more
handsome than his younger brother Eddard.

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:53.879
Brandon did not want to marry Catelyn,
but Lord Rickard's ambitions did not allow

00:03:53.879 --> 00:04:00.200
him to marry the daughter of a northern bannermen.
In 281 AC, Brandon was present at the tourney

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:03.409
at Harrenhal.
There, he was introduced to the crannogman

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:08.359
Howland Reed by his sister, Lyanna.
During the opening feast of the tourney, Brandon

00:04:08.359 --> 00:04:14.040
asked Ashara Dayne, sister of Ser Arthur Dayne,
to dance with Eddard, who was too shy to ask

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:20.739
her himself. Brandon later entered the lists,
but was unhorsed by Prince Rhaegar Targaryen.

00:04:20.739 --> 00:04:25.010
After Prince Rhaegar won the tournament,
he crowned Brandon's sister Lyanna as his

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:28.550
queen of love and beauty, passing over his
own wife,

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:33.530
Princess Elia Martell. Brandon had to be restrained
from confronting Rhaegar,

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:37.210
as he took Rhaegar's action as a slight upon
Lyanna's honor,

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:41.639
since Lyanna had been betrothed to Lord Robert
Baratheon for a long time.

00:04:41.639 --> 00:04:47.030
In 282 AC, Brandon was present at Riverrun
when the date for his wedding to Catelyn was

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:52.419
announced. Petyr Baelish, the ward of Catelyn's
father, Lord Hoster Tully, challenged Brandon

00:04:52.419 --> 00:04:57.920
to a duel for her hand. They fought in the
lower bailey at Riverrun. Catelyn begged him

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:02.490
to spare Petyr's life,
and Brandon promised her to do so. Brandon

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:07.430
armored himself for battle,
aided by Catelyn's young brother, Edmure Tully,

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:12.270
who served as Brandon's squire.
When Brandon saw that Petyr wore only a helm

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:16.360
and a breastplate, and mail,
he took off most of his own armor. Brandon

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:19.389
was more than a match for the much younger
Petyr.

00:05:19.389 --> 00:05:24.220
He offered the boy several chances to yield,
but when Petyr kept refusing,

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:29.479
Brandon ended the duel by injuring Petyr severely.
He defeated Baelish easily,

00:05:29.479 --> 00:05:34.810
nearly disemboweling him in the process, but
Catelyn begged Brandon to spare his life.

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:38.580
The maesters were able to save Baelish and
he eventually recovered,

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:43.849
but he was left with a deep scar running from
his stomach to his collarbone (under his clothes),

00:05:43.849 --> 00:05:48.229
a "token" from Brandon that Baelish would
always carry with him.

00:05:48.229 --> 00:05:53.819
Afterwards he departed Riverrun, promising
Catelyn to return soon so they could wed.

00:05:53.819 --> 00:05:59.199
From Riverrun, Brandon left to join his father's
wedding party, coming down from the north.

00:05:59.199 --> 00:06:03.550
They were on their way again back to Riverrun
for the wedding when the word reached Brandon

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:07.599
of Lyanna's supposed abduction by Prince Rhaegar
Targaryen.

00:06:07.599 --> 00:06:13.830
Brandon, along with his squire Ethan Glover,
Kyle Royce, Elbert Arryn, and Jeffory Mallister,

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:19.069
rode to King's Landing immediately. Upon entering
the Red Keep, Brandon shouted for Rhaegar

00:06:19.069 --> 00:06:24.419
to "come out and die". Rhaegar was not present,
however, and Brandon and his companions were

00:06:24.419 --> 00:06:30.000
arrested by King Aerys II Targaryen and charged
with plotting Rhaegar's murder.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.919
Their fathers were called to court to answer
the charges.

00:06:33.919 --> 00:06:39.800
Aerys II imprisoned Brandon and ordered that
Rickard rides south to answer for his son's

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:44.970
impertinence. Against advice, Rickard agreed,
assuming that the matter would be settled

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:48.879
through a trial
or a bargain of some kind. Brandon was killed

00:06:48.879 --> 00:06:54.300
on the order of Aerys Targaryen, along with
his father, after they protested the kidnapping

00:06:54.300 --> 00:08:26.319
of Lyanna by Prince Rhaegar Targaryen.
Brandon was placed in a strangle device from

00:08:26.319 --> 00:08:30.150
Tyrosh, with a longsword placed just out of
reach.

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:34.630
He was forced to watch as his father was burned
alive in his own armor

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:39.419
and strangled himself while attempting to
get to the sword so he could save his father.

00:08:39.419 --> 00:08:44.890
He was twenty years old at the time. Aerys
then ordered Jon Arryn to hand over his ward

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:50.590
and new Lord of Winterfell Eddard Stark as
well as Robert Baratheon, Lord of Storm's

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:54.440
End.
Having sworn a sacred oath to protect Eddard,

00:08:54.440 --> 00:09:00.820
Jon instead rose his banners in rebellion.
He was supported by the North, Lyanna's betrothed

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:04.970
Robert Baratheon, and Hoster Tully.
This sparked the beginning of the war known

00:09:04.970 --> 00:09:08.320
as Robert's Rebellion,
which led to the near-destruction of House

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:14.900
Targaryen and its removal from the Iron Throne.
Brandon was buried in the crypts beneath Winterfell.

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:19.630
Although only the kings and lords of Winterfell
normally have statues in their likeness placed

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:25.390
beside their tombs, both Brandon and his sister
Lyanna were given a statue by their brother

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:28.720
Eddard,
as he'd loved them very much. Eddard Stark

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:34.130
named his second true born son Brandon
(affectionately known as "Bran") in his elder

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:38.350
brother's memory.
Many stories we heard of such as Brandon almost

00:09:38.350 --> 00:09:42.281
killing Littlefinger,
the Mad King executing Brandon and his father

00:09:42.281 --> 00:09:45.850
Rickard Stark,
many battles we heard of such as the Battle

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:49.630
of the Trident
and the legendary duel between Robert and

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:53.350
Rhaegar during Robert's Rebellion,
all of that and more we'll finally see in

00:09:53.350 --> 00:09:58.040
the upcoming Game of Thrones prequel, House
of the Dragon, coming in 2022 on HBO.

00:09:58.040 --> 00:09:59.040
Let me know your thoughts about everything
in the comment section down below.

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:04.630
Thank you so much for watching and hope to
see you in the next one.

00:10:04.630 --> 00:10:05.090
Peace!

